    (:task
      :id "Task46906" :parentId "" :phase "phase-469"
      :title "Measure whether seeing each other prevents anything"
      :kind :verification :state :planned :lane "effect" :priority :critical :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789300000000 :updatedAt 1789300000000
      :motivation "Cross agent observability is plausible and unmeasured, and it costs every peer a subscription and every write a publication. This programme has already produced one confident conclusion that direct measurement reversed. The collision rate is measurable: two agents given overlapping work, with and without visibility."
      :purpose "The same overlapping task pair runs with the room visible and hidden, and the difference is recorded: writes lost, conflicts raised, work repeated, and tasks completed. A null result is recorded and acted on, and the cost in events and calls is counted against whatever benefit appears."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A measured collision rate with and without visibility" "Lost writes and repeated work counted, not estimated" "The cost counted against the benefit" "A null result recorded"]
      :owns ["asl/bench" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["grading" "concepts" "parallel"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46902" "Task46904" "Task46304"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46906"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46906.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The two arms differ only in whether the room is visible." "A lost write is detected by comparing the tree, not by asking an agent." "A result showing no improvement passes the gate and is recorded."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46906" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Construct the overlapping pair." "Run both arms." "Count outcomes and cost." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46907" :parentId "" :phase "phase-469"
      :title "Ad hoc composition: the agent builds the question it needs"
      :kind :tooling :state :planned :lane "subscription" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789301000000 :updatedAt 1789301000000
      :motivation "No fixed set of queries anticipates what an agent will want to know, and adding a command per question is how a tool surface grows until it costs as much as the log it replaced. The alternative is composition: a short script or a pipe of existing operations folds the data outside the model and only the result crosses into context. The batch rpc form already demonstrates the shape by answering several questions in one roundtrip."
      :purpose "An agent composes a one off query over the event spool and the module graph from the operations that exist, in one roundtrip, with the reduction performed outside the model. The composition is bounded, its output is capped, it states when it truncated, and a composition whose result would be a log rather than an answer is refused rather than served."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Ad hoc composition over spool and graph" "Reduction outside the model" "Bounded output that reports truncation" "A log shaped result refused"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn" "asl/packages/asl-sh/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["rpc"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "bounded" "budget"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46902" "Task46703"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46907"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46907.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A question with no dedicated command is answered by composition in one roundtrip." "A composition whose result would exceed the bound is truncated and says so." "A composition returning raw events rather than a reduction is refused."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46907" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Allow composition over spool and graph." "Bound and report truncation." "Refuse log shaped results." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])]
  :notes "The swarm layer is built and mostly passing. What is absent is narrow: a peer cannot say what it is holding, nothing watches the disk, nothing is resident to hold a room, and the branching merge written for exactly this collision problem has never been connected to a real write.")
